{"name":"Blue Oblivion","hex":"#26428b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"oblivion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of forgetting completely, of being oblivious, unconscious, unaware, as when sleeping, drunk, or dead.","The state of being completely forgotten, of being reduced to a state of non-existence, extinction, or nothingness, including through war and destruction.  for an area like hell, a wasteland."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consign to oblivion; to efface utterly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oblivion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oblivion (2013 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Oblivion is a 2013 American epic post-apocalyptic science fiction action film produced and directed by Joseph Kosinski from a screenplay by Karl Gajdusek and Michael deBruyn, starring Tom Cruise in the main role alongside Morgan Freeman, Olga Kurylenko, Andrea Riseborough, Nikolaj Coster-Waldau, and Melissa Leo in supporting roles. Based on Kosinski's unpublished Radical Comics graphic novel of the same name, the film pays homage to 1970s sci-fi, and is a \"love story\" set in 2077 on a post-apocalyptic Earth desolated by an alien war. A maintenance technician (Cruise) on the verge of completing his mission recovers a woman (Kurylenko) who survived a space pod crash, leading him to question his purpose and discover the truth about the war."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Oblivion2013Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oblivion_(2013_film)","wikidata":"Q638544"},{"title":"Oblivion (roller coaster)","blocks":[{"text":"Oblivion is a steel roller coaster at the Alton Towers theme park in Staffordshire, England. Marketed as the \"world's first vertical drop roller coaster\", it was manufactured by Bolliger & Mabillard as the first Dive Coaster."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/Oblivion_rollercoaster_logo.png/330px-Oblivion_rollercoaster_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oblivion_(roller_coaster)","wikidata":"Q1476808"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/Oblivion_BubbleShip.jpg/330px-Oblivion_BubbleShip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/Oblivion_BubbleShip.jpg/330px-Oblivion_BubbleShip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"h